# Purity of real sheaves on curves

Purity for a real sheaf on a curve over a finite field: the weight statement that is the
geometric heart of Weil II. It is deduced from the trace formula, Poincaré duality,
smooth purity and the algebraic monodromy statements of
`WeilConjectures.Blueprint.AlgebraicGroupsLieAlgebras`.

Blueprint block `sec-purity-real-sheaves`.
-/
